    s__SIM_HOW_TO_REPLY(py_str("Power the phone off first, then push a paperclip or the pin that came with it into the pinhole beside the tray until it clicks and the tray slides out. The card sits in the outline with its cut corner matching the diagram on the tray, gold contacts down, and it only fits one way, so do not force it: an adapter that is too thin is the usual reason a card will not seat, and a strip of tape on the back of it fixes that. Slide the tray in flat until it is flush, then switch on and wait a minute; if it still asks for a SIM, check in Settings > Mobile Data that the plan is switched on there."));
    s__SIM_FAULT_REPLY(py_str("Power the phone right off, then open the SIM tray with a paperclip, take the card out and wipe the gold contacts with a dry cloth before putting it back the same way round - a card that has worked for months has usually just shifted. If the phone takes an eSIM, check in Settings > Mobile Data that the plan has not been deleted. After that, look for a carrier settings update and then Settings > General > Transfer or Reset > Reset > Reset Network Settings, which clears the network record without touching your data; a phone that still says no SIM after that has a failed tray or reader, and the network's shop will test it with their own card in a minute."));
